{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 84, :comments ["<b>On the day it was anointed, etc.</b> Here our words that we wrote above are vindicated — that they all brought their offerings together on a single day, except that their gift was arranged one per day." "<b>From the princes of Israel.</b> One must know why it was necessary to say so. And perhaps Scripture praises them that of their own they performed the dedication of the altar, and the phrase <b>from the princes of</b> means from them the deed came, and they had no need to draw from others. And our Sages of blessed memory said (Sifrei Numbers 53) that it comes to say that all of them were equal in one commandment and one merit, end quote. The meaning of their saying 'one merit' is with respect to the offering spoken of in the matter, but among them gradations may be found — one above another — for Nahshon was greater than them all."], :book :numbers, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T20:06:47.767874886Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}